WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.092
Arctic

00:00:01.246 --> 00:00:02.567
a practical lock-free

00:00:02.378 --> 00:00:03.805
adaptive radix tree

00:00:04.326 --> 00:00:05.729
UT Austin and

00:00:05.623 --> 00:00:07.238
ETH Zurich researchers

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.076
present Arctic

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.467
a lock-free adaptive

00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:10.281
radix tree that

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:11.425
pairs high performance

00:00:11.236 --> 00:00:12.392
with range scans

00:00:12.203 --> 00:00:13.500
and beats lock-based

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:14.066
indexes

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.375
including a concurrent

00:00:15.187 --> 00:00:16.024
hash map

00:00:16.154 --> 00:00:17.498
on many YCSB

00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:18.064
setups

00:00:18.598 --> 00:00:20.437
Arctic guarantees non-blocking

00:00:20.249 --> 00:00:21.876
operation through careful

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.055
metadata layout and

00:00:22.879 --> 00:00:24.553
a freezing-based coordination

00:00:24.364 --> 00:00:25.154
protocol

00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:27.182
and offers non-linearizable

00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:28.385
range and prefix

00:00:28.197 --> 00:00:28.951
scans

00:00:29.486 --> 00:00:30.417
Swapped in for

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:31.349
the default skiplist

00:00:31.161 --> 00:00:31.915
indexes

00:00:32.057 --> 00:00:33.059
it raised throughput

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.356
on write-heavy benchmarks

00:00:34.179 --> 00:00:34.769
by up to

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.537
40% in RocksDB

00:00:36.349 --> 00:00:37.693
and 12% in

00:00:37.505 --> 00:00:38.153
Turso

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:39.684
Full story on

00:00:39.495 --> 00:00:40.391
the dashboard
